# A ball with a 2-limb center from an interval [lo, hi] of two values of T supplied by the
# program (guarded, rule R3). The center is lo/2 + hi/2 as an exact 2-limb number, by two_sum_ord;
# the radius is RU(hi/2 - lo/2), the smallest radius of T for that center. When a halving is not
# exact (a bound that is an odd multiple of eta) the center may be off by eta, and the radius is
# the number after RN(RU(hi/2 - lo/2) + eta). States: the empty set when lo <= hi is false (lo > hi,
# or a NaN) or lo = +inf or hi = -inf; the whole line when a bound is infinite.
kernel:        ball_from_interval_2
input:         lo
input:         hi
output:        cw = cw0 cw1
output:        rw
status:        unverified
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   unverified
entry:         yes
ieee_only:     yes
cone_exempt:   every output is selected after explicit tests of the bounds

gl       = guard(lo)
gu       = guard(hi)
hl       = prod(gl, const up(1/2))
hu       = prod(gu, const up(1/2))
(c0, c1) = two_sum_ord(hl, hu)
d        = sub_up_1(hu, hl)
bl       = add(hl, hl)
bu       = add(hu, hu)
xl       = eq(bl, gl)
xu       = eq(bu, gu)
xx       = and(xl, xu)
da       = add(d, const up(eta))
dn       = succ(da)
r        = select(xx, d, dn)
ok       = le(gl, gu)
nl       = lt(gl, const inf)
mi       = neg(const inf)
nu       = lt(mi, gu)
va       = and(ok, nl)
v        = and(va, nu)
fl       = lt(mi, gl)
fu       = lt(gu, const inf)
f        = and(fl, fu)
k0       = select(f, c0, 0)
k1       = select(f, c1, 0)
s        = select(f, r, const inf)
cw0      = select(v, k0, const nan)
cw1      = select(v, k1, const nan)
rw       = select(v, s, const nan)
